  "note": "Three hand-authored personas for the Eye Prescription classification engine. classify(state) returns per-eye sphere/cylinder classes ('' when the dioptre value is null), presbyopiaClass (null adds coerce to 0 via ||, so 'none' - never ''), anisometropia (|R-L| sphere, null if either is null), prismPresent, complexity (worst-of: any high band / prism / aniso > 2.00 -> 'complex'; any presbyopia or moderate band -> 'moderate'; else 'simple' - so an all-null prescription is 'simple'), firedRules (audit trail in fixed order: R sphere, L sphere, R cyl, L cyl, add, R-ANISO-01 when aniso > 0.50, R-PRISM-01) and additionalFlags FOLDED in. Flags are NOT priority-sorted: insertion order, with flagId F-<CATEGORY>-<NNN> numbered by a single running counter across all categories (so F-PRESBYOPIA-005 is legal). Quirks verified: R-ANISO-01 fires above 0.50 D but the anisometropia flag only above 2.00 D; significant-change uses a strict > 1.00 D so an exact 1.00 D shift is silent; prescription-expired compares new Date(expiryDate) (midnight UTC) against the frozen clock 2026-09-03T12:00Z, so an expiry dated today already counts as expired; grade.overrideComplexity is applied only by form-app.js at render time and never changes result.complexity; classifySphere has a latent gap for off-grid spheres strictly between -0.75 and -0.50 (they fall to 'low-hyperopia'), unreachable through the UI's 0.25 D snapping. No wall-clock keys in the result. Regenerate expected with: bin/test-personas eye-prescription --update",
